# ComposeUX SVG Rendering [SPEC:CXC-SVG]

> SVG is a core rendering capability, not an optional extension ([CXC-R-DRAW-SVG]). The engine parses SVG into Layer-1 Canvas drawing commands, so anything that emits SVG — a stylized "Red Alert", Mermaid, Graphviz, D3, matplotlib — renders on every ComposeUX surface through the one contract.

---

## 1. Intent

### [CXC-SVG-INTENT] Decompose SVG to the Drawing Contract

- definition: The engine includes a platform-independent SVG parser that converts an SVG document into `Canvas` primitive calls (paths, rects, circles, text, fills, strokes, gradients, transforms, clips). The Canvas backend then draws them like anything else.
- key-insight: Because SVG decomposes to the *existing* Canvas contract, it renders on every backend for free — Skia (crisp), CanvasKit (browser), and the CYD (subject to its primitive subset). Crisp vector text (a stylized "Red Alert") and every diagram tool become universally renderable.
- status: planned
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-SVG]

---

## 2. Parser Contract

### [CXC-SVG-PARSER] Element → Primitive Mapping

- definition: a platform-independent parser (Python, shared) maps SVG elements to Canvas calls per the [CXC-R-DRAW-SVG] table:
  - `rect`→`fill_rect`/`fill_round_rect`; `circle`→`fill/stroke_circle`; `ellipse`→`fill_path` (arc-approx); `line`→`draw_line`; `polyline`/`polygon`→`draw/fill_path`; `path`→`draw/fill_path` (M,L,C,Q,A,Z); `text`→`draw_text`+`set_font`; `image`→`draw_image` (href via asset manager); `g`→`save`/`restore` with group transform; `defs`/`use`→parse-time inline expansion; `linearGradient`/`radialGradient`→`set_linear/radial_gradient`; `clipPath`→`clip_rect`/path clip.
- attributes: `fill`, `stroke`, `stroke-width`, `opacity`, `transform` (translate/rotate/scale/matrix) map to style + transform state. (`transform` uses the transform ops added for [SPEC:CXC-BIND].)
- coverage: the above element + attribute set is the conformance target ([CXC-R-C14]); unsupported features degrade to a warning, not a crash.
- test: a reference SVG exercising every mapped element renders correctly and pixel-identically macOS↔RPi.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-SVG]

### [CXC-SVG-TIERS] Portability & the CYD Subset

- role: Skia/CanvasKit render the full mapping. The CYD's `ESP32Canvas` implements a primitive *subset* (no fill_arc/paths/transforms yet — M5), so complex SVG (arbitrary paths, gradients, transforms) degrades on the CYD until M5 fills those primitives; simple SVG (rects/circles/lines/text) renders now.
- test: a simple SVG renders on the CYD; a path-heavy SVG is flagged as degraded, not crashed.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-SVG]

---

## 3. Widget & Assets

### [CXC-SVG-WIDGET] SvgWidget

- role: an `SvgWidget` renders an SVG referenced as `src: doc://…/x.svg` or `bus://assets/…/x.svg` (asset manager, cached), scaled to its rect (fit modes as Image). A bound `src` swaps the graphic reactively ([SPEC:CXC-BIND]).
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-SVG]

---

## 4. Diagram Pipeline

### [CXC-SVG-DIAGRAM] Mermaid/Graphviz → SVG → Any Surface

- flow: diagram text (in `.compose.yaml` or a referenced doc) → a **diagram service** (hub workload running Mermaid.js/Graphviz in Node) renders it to SVG → the SVG is stored in document_store → an SvgWidget references `doc://diagrams/{id}.svg` and renders it. When the diagram source changes, the service re-renders and the widget updates (config poll or bus event).
- role: the diagram service is a simple hub workload — it watches for diagram text in bus_storage, renders, stores. This is the [CXC-R-C15] pipeline.
- pan/zoom: a DiagramView variant supports pan/zoom (pinch on touch, scroll on desktop) — [CXC-R-C16].
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-SVG]

---

## 5. Compliance

| ID | Requirement | Testable Criterion |
|----|-------------|-------------------|
| CXC-SVG-C1 | SVG via primitives | An SVG renders using drawing primitives on Skia + RPi, pixel-identical ([CXC-R-C13]) |
| CXC-SVG-C2 | Element coverage | rect/circle/ellipse/line/poly/path(M,L,C,Q,A,Z)/text/image/g/defs/use/gradients/clip all render ([CXC-R-C14]) |
| CXC-SVG-C3 | Bound src | An SvgWidget with a namespace-bound `src` swaps graphics reactively |
| CXC-SVG-C4 | Red Alert (crisp) | A stylized "Red Alert" authored as SVG renders crisp at large scale (no raster upscaling) |
| CXC-SVG-C5 | Mermaid pipeline | Mermaid text → diagram service → SVG in doc_store → widget displays it ([CXC-R-C15]) |
| CXC-SVG-C6 | Diagram pan/zoom | DiagramView pans/zooms smoothly on touch + desktop ([CXC-R-C16]) |
| CXC-SVG-C7 | CYD degradation | A simple SVG renders on the CYD; a path-heavy one degrades with a warning, not a crash |

